OL,3,GNEWSASex offenders face
OL,4,Aliving-in-a-council home ban
OL,5,
OL,6,FConvicted sex offenders will be banned
OL,7,Ffrom a council home under new plans set
OL,8,Ffor consideration in Warwickshire.
OL,10,FThe Reform UK-run cabinet at Nuneaton
OL,11,Fand Bedworth Borough Council has
OL,12,Fapproved an update to the eligibility
OL,13,Fcriteria for those applying for a house
OL,14,Fin the area, although it needs to be
OL,15,Fratified by full council.
OL,17,FAn update to its Housing Allocation
OL,18,FPolicy that says anyone convicted of a
OL,19,Fserious sexual offence would be
OL,20,Fautomatically barred from being
OL,21,Fconsidered.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
